    "bio": "I am a Doctoral Researcher at the <a href=\"https://web.umons.ac.be/en/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">University of Mons (UMONS)</a>, supervised by <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/nicolasgillis\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">Prof. Nicolas Gillis</a>. My current research sits at the intersection of Matrix Theory and Optimization, specifically developing matrix factorization and low-rank approximation methods for Trustworthy Machine Learning. I aim to leverage these mathematical tools to enhance robustness, interpretability, and fairness in high-dimensional data and network analysis.<br><br>Previously, I was a Graduate Research Assistant at the <a href=\"https://uok.ac.ir/en/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">University of Kurdistan</a>, where I led the <a href=\"https://amlteams.github.io/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">Algebraic Machine Learning (AML) team</a> and focused on representation learning.",
